hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16179","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Attaf narrated to us, he said: Mujammi ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from a boy of the people of Quba that he reached him old, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us at Quba and sat in the shade of al-Ahmar, and people gathered to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink, was given drink, and drank, and I was on his right, and I was the youngest of the people, so he handed to me and I drank. And I remembered that he prayed with us that day with his sandals on, he did not remove them."
